                        <Interaction>
                            <Abbreviated/>
                            <Professional>Salicylates may reduce the beneficial effects of angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitors (ACEIs). Salicylates inhibit synthesis of prostaglandins and may antagonise antihypertensive effects of ACEIs in a dose-dependent manner, cause vasoconstriction/reduced cardiac output in heart failure patients, as well as increased risk of renal impairment. However, studies have shown that low-dose aspirin (less than or equals to 100 mg per day) is less likely to interact with ACEI. Furthermore, there are conflicting results of aspirin’s effect to worsen heart failure in patients on concomitant ACEI. Nevertheless, if concurrent use is necessary, monitor patient’s clinical condition, blood pressure and renal function.</Professional>
